# Security Standards

## Principle of Least Privilege

- Request only `storage`, `activeTab`, `scripting` permissions
- Content script matches `https://www.linkedin.com/*` only
- No `<all_urls>` or broad host permissions

## Data Restrictions

- All processing local — no network transmission
- No analytics, tracking, or telemetry
- Do not log email addresses or user keywords

## Input Validation

- Validate email format before storing: `/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/`
- Sanitize user input before DOM insertion (use `textContent`, not `innerHTML`)
- Confirm destructive actions with `confirm()` dialog

## Permission Review

When adding new Chrome permissions:
1. Justify in `docs/MANIFEST.md`
2. Update Chrome Web Store listing text
3. Update `docs/PRIVACY_AND_SECURITY.md`
